<h4 data-start=3D"5143" data-end=3D"5162" class=3D"">3.1 Composants</h4>
<p data-start=3D"5164" data-end=3D"5380" class=3D"">Les <strong data-start=
=3D"5168" data-end=3D"5182">composants</strong> sont l'=C3=A9l=C3=A9ment ce=
ntral d'une application Angular. Ils contiennent la logique de l'interface =
utilisateur et sont responsables du rendu du HTML. Un composant se compose =
de trois parties principales :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"5382" data-end=3D"5596">
<li data-start=3D"5382" data-end=3D"5453" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5384" data-end=3D"5453" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
384" data-end=3D"5399">Le template</strong> (HTML) : D=C3=A9crit l'interfac=
e utilisateur du composant.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5454" data-end=3D"5525" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5456" data-end=3D"5525" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
456" data-end=3D"5469">La classe</strong> (TypeScript) : Contient la logiqu=
e m=C3=A9tier du composant.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5526" data-end=3D"5596" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5528" data-end=3D"5596" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
528" data-end=3D"5542">Les styles</strong> (CSS) : Stylise l'interface util=
isateur du composant.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"5598" data-end=3D"5624" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
598" data-end=3D"5622">Exemple de composant</strong> :</p>
