<h4 data-start=3D"5872" data-end=3D"5891" class=3D"">3.2 Directives</h4>
<p data-start=3D"5893" data-end=3D"6005" class=3D"">Les <strong data-start=
=3D"5897" data-end=3D"5911">directives</strong> permettent de manipuler le =
DOM de mani=C3=A8re d=C3=A9clarative. Angular propose plusieurs directives =
:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"6007" data-end=3D"6224">
<li data-start=3D"6007" data-end=3D"6102" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6009" data-end=3D"6102" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
009" data-end=3D"6037">Directives structurelles</strong> : Elles changent l=
a structure du DOM, comme <code data-start=3D"6082" data-end=3D"6089">*ngIf=
</code> et <code data-start=3D"6093" data-end=3D"6101">*ngFor</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6103" data-end=3D"6224" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6105" data-end=3D"6224" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
105" data-end=3D"6131">Directives d'attributs</strong> : Elles modifient l'=
apparence ou le comportement d'un =C3=A9l=C3=A9ment, comme <code data-start=
=3D"6201" data-end=3D"6210">ngClass</code> et <code data-start=3D"6214" dat=
a-end=3D"6223">ngStyle</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"6226" data-end=3D"6271" class=3D"">3.3 Services et Inject=
ion de D=C3=A9pendances</h4>
