<h3 data-start=3D"8915" data-end=3D"8939" class=3D"">5.2 Bonnes Pratiques</=
h3>
<ul data-start=3D"8941" data-end=3D"9339">
<li data-start=3D"8941" data-end=3D"9024" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"8943" data-end=3D"9024" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"8=
943" data-end=3D"8957">Modularit=C3=A9</strong> : Divisez votre application=
 en composants petits et r=C3=A9utilisables.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"9025" data-end=3D"9145" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"9027" data-end=3D"9145" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"9=
027" data-end=3D"9052">Responsabilit=C3=A9 unique</strong> : Un composant d=
oit avoir une seule responsabilit=C3=A9. Ne le surchargez pas de fonctionna=
lit=C3=A9s.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"9146" data-end=3D"9230" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"9148" data-end=3D"9230" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"9=
148" data-end=3D"9162">Lisibilit=C3=A9</strong> : Nommez vos composants et =
m=C3=A9thodes de mani=C3=A8re explicite et claire.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"9231" data-end=3D"9339" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"9233" data-end=3D"9339" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"9=
233" data-end=3D"9242">Tests</strong> : R=C3=A9digez des tests unitaires po=
ur chaque composant afin de garantir la stabilit=C3=A9 de votre code.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"9341" data-end=3D"9344" class=3D"">
