<li data-start=3D"4565" data-end=3D"5213" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4568" data-end=3D"4737" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
568" data-end=3D"4579">Payload</strong> : C'est un objet JSON qui contient =
les donn=C3=A9es que vous voulez encoder dans le token. Ces donn=C3=A9es so=
nt appel=C3=A9es "claims". Elles peuvent =C3=AAtre de trois types :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4741" data-end=3D"5086">
<li data-start=3D"4741" data-end=3D"4855" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4743" data-end=3D"4855" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
743" data-end=3D"4764">Registered claims</strong> : Claims pr=C3=A9d=C3=A9f=
inies, comme <code data-start=3D"4793" data-end=3D"4798">iss</code> (issuer=
), <code data-start=3D"4809" data-end=3D"4814">exp</code> (expiration time)=
, <code data-start=3D"4834" data-end=3D"4839">sub</code> (subject), etc.</p=
>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4859" data-end=3D"4964" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4861" data-end=3D"4964" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
861" data-end=3D"4878">Public claims</strong> : Claims d=C3=A9finies librem=
ent mais qui doivent =C3=AAtre uniques pour =C3=A9viter les collisions.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4968" data-end=3D"5086" class=3D"">
