<h2 data-start=3D"7304" data-end=3D"7348" class=3D"">6. Gestion des Asserti=
ons dans Protractor</h2>
<p data-start=3D"7350" data-end=3D"7533" class=3D"">Protractor utilise <str=
ong data-start=3D"7369" data-end=3D"7380">Jasmine</strong> pour les asserti=
ons dans les tests E2E. Voici quelques assertions courantes que vous pouvez=
 utiliser pour v=C3=A9rifier le comportement de votre application.</p>
<ul data-start=3D"7535" data-end=3D"7767">
<li data-start=3D"7535" data-end=3D"7603" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7537" data-end=3D"7603" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
537" data-end=3D"7571"><code data-start=3D"7539" data-end=3D"7569">expect(e=
lement).toBeTruthy()</code></strong> : V=C3=A9rifie que l'=C3=A9l=C3=A9ment=
 existe.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7604" data-end=3D"7677" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7606" data-end=3D"7677" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
606" data-end=3D"7639"><code data-start=3D"7608" data-end=3D"7637">expect(e=
lement).toBeFalsy()</code></strong> : V=C3=A9rifie que l'=C3=A9l=C3=A9ment =
n'existe pas.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7678" data-end=3D"7767" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7680" data-end=3D"7767" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
680" data-end=3D"7713"><code data-start=3D"7682" data-end=3D"7711">expect(e=
lement).toContain()</code></strong> : V=C3=A9rifie qu'un =C3=A9l=C3=A9ment =
contient un texte sp=C3=A9cifique.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"7769" data-end=3D"7772" class=3D"">
